## Hairstyles as portraiture

From 1968, the photographer J. D. 'Okhai Ojeikere documented Nigerian hairstyles, shot from behind and in profile. Hair becomes sculpture, and each portrait records how people chose to present themselves.

It shows how an everyday subject can hold a whole culture's craft.

Demonstration copy. Confirm dates and captions with his estate or a museum source before publishing. No Ojeikere photographs are shown here.

